30,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"We are losing critical internal knowledge and trainers aren't sticking. We need a vendor that provides deep, on-site support during the transition.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Kenji,,Our yards are a mess of old gear and we can't stop for a cutover in winter. We need something that actually works with old hardware.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"It seems the board prefers operating expenses over capital. Also, separate licenses are a financial trap; bundled pricing is much more stable.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"It's just as I feared! Support is a mess of finger-pointing, and our initial plans never survive the first year. We need a single point of accountability.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,It appears we have a habit of neglecting upgrades and suffering from poor external data migrations. A system that ages gracefully or is managed internally is preferable.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Yumi, if support is that fragmented, we definitely can't afford a complex modular system that requires us to manage multiple vendors.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if we can't do big upgrades, maybe we need something that doesn't require us to overhaul everything at once?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Misaki, @Yumi, if we want stability in cost and support, a bundled, hosted suite seems more logical than separate components.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"I agree with Toshio! We need one throat to choke when things break, and a system that can adapt when the business changes.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the risk is that ""not overhauling"" leads to the stagnation I found. However, a vendor with an engineering team on-site might mitigate the migration risks.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"On-site presence is key. If the depot supervisors ignore outside trainers, we need someone there for the long haul.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"Exactly! If the system is too ""modern"" for our old scanners, the guys in the yard will just go back to spreadsheets.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"We must avoid the ""add-on"" price creep. A fixed configuration or a subscription with a clear cap is the only way to protect the budget.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"So we need a partner who handles the training and the migration, and doesn't just hand us a manual and leave.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,It seems we are leaning toward a solution that balances stability with high-touch implementation. Let us see the candidates.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
