55,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Anchor's engineering team being present through rollout is exactly what we need for the supervisors and the staffing gap.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Kenji,,Anchor is built for transport operators. That sounds like it would actually survive our yards and the peak-season chaos.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Corvus is out; separate licenses are a cost nightmare. Meridian's fixed configuration and bundled suite are financially safer.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Meridian offers a hosted suite with a regional team, which solves the support ownership issue. But Tessera's configurable workflows help with the changing rules.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Tessera relies on a partner firm for migration—that's exactly how we got the 2018 data mess. Anchor's on-site team is more reliable.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Toshio, would Anchor's on-premise model be a capital request problem?","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"I don't care about the servers, I just want it to work in the yard! Anchor sounds like the most rugged choice.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Misaki, it might be, but the maintenance cost is usually lower than the yearly creep of a subscription or modular licenses.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"I'm torn. Meridian is stable, but Anchor's presence during rollout solves the ""nobody in charge"" problem I'm worried about.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Anchor's specific focus on transport operators suggests it won't be a ""general"" tool that we have to ring with spreadsheets.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I'm voting Anchor. The human element—the retirements and the supervisors—is the biggest risk.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Kenji,,Me too. Anchor is the only one that feels like it's made for the depot floor.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"While Meridian is a safe financial bet, Anchor's outright purchase model avoids the recurring price hikes I found in the invoices.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"If everyone is leaning toward Anchor for the support and rollout, I'll join in. We can't afford another failed rollout.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,Logic dictates that the highest risk is implementation and technical obsolescence. Anchor addresses both.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
